# Cursor ML scope (hard rules)

## Read-only UI / deploy / ops files

Cursor must **NOT modify** these files (read-only only):

- `New for anti/app.js`
- `New for anti/style.css`
- `New for anti/index.html`
- `New for anti/data.js`
- `New for anti/shipping.js`
- `_worker.js`
- `wrangler.jsonc`
- `.github/workflows/**`
- `CLAUDE.md`
- `docs/ops/OWNERS.md`
- `docs/ops/TASKS.md`

## Branch discipline

- Never change git branches without asking the user first.
- **NEVER** checkout `claude/*` branches.
- Stay on the current ML branch; switch only when the user explicitly authorizes it.

## Allowed Cursor work scope (ML / model only)

- `New for anti/scripts/yield_model/**` (including `{country}/model.yaml`)
- `public/data/*_yield_forecast.json` and `New for anti/public/data/*_yield_forecast.json` (respect `New for anti/scripts/yield_model/DATA_LAYOUT.md`)

## Country → screen (no UI edit)

Do **not** wire countries via `CLIMATE_COUNTRIES` in `app.js`. Use:

```bash
cd "New for anti/scripts/yield_model"
python3 scaffold_manifest.py {country}   # fill iso / label_ko / label_en / sources
python3 build_registry.py --check        # validate only; do not commit climate_registry_v1.json
```

See `MODEL_MANIFEST.md` and rule `climate-manifest-no-appjs`.

## Git hygiene

- Never stage or commit `.verify_live/` (Chrome profile junk).
- Never commit `public/data/climate_registry_v1.json` from a country PR (CI regenerates on main).
